# docs/28 §3.5 (S1a): handed to the wrong Mac. The work Mac pulls two memos; in Settings → Storage
# (Opt+M, then `,`) "Send again" asks first (a box on Cancel), then puts them back, never for that
# Mac; "To this Mac" would undo it; the home Mac takes them.
boot store=sd usb=on bat=4100 lang=zh
include work_mac.cpas
wait 600
include memo.cpas
include memo.cpas
pull
press opt+m
press ,
shot storage  Settings → Storage: Send again from ·XXXX: 2, To this Mac none, Clear kept 2 files, the facts
press tab
shot storage-menu  Tab on Storage: its Here rows
press tab
press enter
shot again-box  Enter: Send 2 to another Mac? ·XXXX won't get them again, the cursor on Cancel
press /
press enter
wait 300
shot again  / Enter: Queued again: 2; To sync 2, nothing kept; To this Mac 2 files
pull
shot not-here  the work Mac pulls again: nothing (still To sync 2)
usb off
wait 1500
usb on
include home_mac.cpas
wait 6000
pull
press opt+m
press ,
shot home  the home Mac took them: kept again, the batch now goes to its ·XXXX
